<title>USA: U.S. House panel approves $209 million SPR sale.</title>
<headline>U.S. House panel approves $209 million SPR sale.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House Appropriations committee Thursday approved a plan to sell $209 million worth of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve in fiscal 1998, which begins Oct. 1.</p>
<p>Revenue from the oil sale would be used to cover the cost of running the reserve.</p>
<p>The committee said it needed the money because Republican leaders had not allocated enough money to the panel for all of its programs. However, Republicans from the House Commerce Committee, which is in charge of authorizing SPR oil sales, planned to introduce an amendment on the House floor to strip the oil auction out of the bill.</p>
<p>((Washington energy desk, 202 898 8467))</p>
